dium-term commercial loans for working capital, business expansion, and purchase of equipment; commercial business loans; commercial mortgage loans; one-to-four family residential mortgage loans; home improvement loans, closed-end home equity loans, and home equity lines of credit; and consumer loans, such as automobile, secured installment, and other secured and unsecured personal loans, as well as recreational vehicle, boat, personal loans, and deposit account collateralized loans. In addition, it offers investment advisory, wealth management, investment consulting, and retirement plan services, as well as operates a real estate investment trust that holds residential mortgages and commercial real estate loans. Financial Institutions, Inc. was founded in 1817 and is headquartered in Warsaw, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Martin K. Birmingham | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 631 people. Revenue per employee of $388K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $21K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Financial Institutions, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $750M market cap on $245M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $13M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.25\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 2.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 101% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.012035197776288},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 8% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","26 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Financial Institutions (NASDAQ:FISI) Stock Crosses Below 50 Day Moving Average \u2013 What\u2019s Next?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/financial-institutions-nasdaqfisi-stock-crosses-below-50-day-moving-average-whats-next.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794396233.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.856,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (FISI) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/1/Price-Driven_Insight_from_FISI_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_111126061001_1794395401.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794395401.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why (FISI) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/Why_FISI_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_Tactical_Trading_110126061002_1793531402.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793531402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Financial Institutions (FISI) Stock Caught Between Q3 Earnings And Funding Costs","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/financial-institutions-fisi-stock-caught-061721395.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793427441.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Financial Institutions, Inc. Announces January 2027 Dividends: $0.32 Common and Preferred Stock Payouts","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinem